---
import PaperLayout from "../layouts/PaperLayout.astro";
/**
 * /shipping-and-returns/
 *
 * Written 12 September 2026, because the shop was live and taking cards with
 * no stated returns policy at all. Selling at distance to consumers in the
 * EU/EEA from Sweden carries a mandatory 14-day right of withdrawal, and the
 * customer only bears the cost of returning goods if the seller says so
 * BEFORE the purchase. Saying nothing does not mean the customer pays — it
 * means we do. This page is where that is said.
 *
 * Nothing on this page is a promise we cannot keep. Delivery windows are the
 * supplier's real quoted windows, not marketing numbers.
 */
const lastUpdated = "September 12, 2026";
---

<PaperLayout
  title="Shipping and Returns · The Next Cigar"
  description="How long delivery takes, where things ship from, and how to send something back. Fourteen-day right of withdrawal, stated plainly."
  section="legal"
  compact={true}
>
  <div class="dateline">
    <h1>Shipping and Returns</h1>
    <p class="st">Legal · last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
  </div>
  <article class="art">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:720px">
      <h2>Where things ship from</h2>
      <p>
        We sell cigar accessories — cutters, lighters, cases, humidification. We do not sell
        tobacco and never have.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most accessories ship <strong>direct from our supplier</strong> rather than from a
        warehouse of ours. That is how a small shop can carry a range without holding thousands
        of kronor of stock, and we would rather say so than let you assume there is a building
        in Malmö with your cutter in it. It means delivery takes longer than Amazon. It also
        means the price is lower than it would otherwise be.
      </p>

      <h2>How long it takes</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>One to two weeks</strong> to most of Europe and North America, tracked. Each
        product page states its own window where it differs. If something is going to take
        longer than that, we email you rather than let you wonder.
      </p>
      <p>
        Parcels ship from our supplier outside the EU. Inside the EU, VAT is settled when we
        place the order, and since July 2026 there is a flat €3 customs fee per item on small
        parcels from outside the Union; if a carrier asks you for it, or for a handling charge, at
        the door, pay it, send us the receipt, and we refund it in full. Outside the EU, import
        duty and local tax are set by your own country and are not ours to collect or waive.
      </p>

      <h2>Lighters arrive without gas</h2>
      <p>
        Every lighter ships empty. A lighter containing butane is classified as dangerous goods
        (UN 1057, class 2.1) and cannot travel by ordinary air freight; purged and empty, it is
        an ordinary metal object. Fill it with any refined butane refill — a few euros in any
        tobacconist. This is not a defect and it is not us cutting a corner. It is how every
        lighter bought online crosses a border.
      </p>

      <h2>Changing your mind — 14 days</h2>
      <p>
        You have <strong>14 days from the day the goods reach you</strong> to withdraw from the
        purchase, for any reason or none. You do not have to explain yourself and we will not
        ask you to.
      </p>
      <p>
        To withdraw, email <a href="mailto:orders@thenextcigar.com">orders@thenextcigar.com</a>
        with your order number and say you are cancelling. Anything unambiguous counts — you do
        not need a form.
      </p>
      <p>
        Send the goods back within 14 days of telling us. <strong>You pay the cost of return
        postage</strong> unless the item arrived faulty, damaged or not as described, in which
        case we pay it. Use a tracked service; until it reaches us it is still your parcel.
      </p>
      <p>
        We refund within <strong>14 days</strong> of receiving the goods back, to the card you
        paid with. That includes the original standard delivery charge. We may reduce the refund
        if the item has been handled more than you would handle it in a shop — trying a cutter
        is fine, using it for a fortnight is not.
      </p>

      <h2>If something arrives faulty</h2>
      <p>
        Email us with a photograph. We replace it or refund it, your choice, and we pay the
        postage both ways. This right is separate from the 14 days above and lasts far longer —
        under Swedish law you can complain about a faulty product for up to three years.
      </p>

      <h2>What cannot be returned</h2>
      <p>
        Digital products — guides, PDFs — are non-refundable once downloaded, because there is
        nothing to send back. Everything physical can be returned.
      </p>

      <h2>Who you are dealing with</h2>
      <p>
        The Next Cigar is owned and operated by Cristian Ortiz Suárez, Malmö, Sweden. For
        anything to do with an order, email
        <a href="mailto:orders@thenextcigar.com">orders@thenextcigar.com</a>. We answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we cannot resolve a complaint between us, consumers in the EU can take it to the
        <a href="https://www.arn.se/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Allmänna reklamationsnämnden</a>
        (the Swedish National Board for Consumer Disputes) or the EU's online dispute resolution
        platform. We will follow their decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PaperLayout>
